{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>The descendants of Naphtali</b> — in all of them it says \"לבני\" (to the descendants of), except for Naphtali, who says \"בני\" (the descendants of) — because in the tribe of Naphtali there were more daughters than sons. Therefore there is a hint in the blessing of Naphtali: אשה אילה שלוחה הנותן, whose notarikon is אשה. And therefore in the episode of Phinehas, all of them are written \"בני\" — because the men had died and the women multiplied. Therefore it does not say \"לבני.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:01.415960391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}